%N A399212 Number of solutions to x^2 + 9*y^2 = n in positive integers x and y.
%H A399212 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A399212/b399212.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A399212 G.f.: (theta_3(q) - 1)*(theta_3(q^9) - 1)/4, where theta_3() is the Jacobi theta function. - _Ilya Gutkovskiy_, Sep 03 2026
%o A399212 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 0, sum(k=1, sqrtint((n-1)\9), issquare(n-9*k^2)));
